# Only client-side routes get rewritten to the app shell. The router's base is
# /pos/, so scoping the rewrite there is enough.
#
# Crucially this must NOT be a global /* catch-all: that swallowed requests for
# missing hashed assets and answered them with index.html as 200 text/html.
# Assets carry a long max-age, so browsers then cached an HTML document under a
# .css URL and the Tables route's dynamic import rejected on it. With no rule
# matching /assets/*, Pages falls through to 404.html with a real 404 status,
# which is not cached as content and fails loudly instead of silently.
/pos/*  /index.html  200
